{"nodes": [{"id": "keepqueue_server_readme_keepqueue_server", "label": "Keepqueue Server Application", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "keepqueue-server/README.md", "source_location": "Overview", "source_url": "https://keepqueue.com/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Node.js + Express + TypeScript API layer over Firebase. README says the server starts on a configured port defaulting to 3000, while CLAUDE.md documents the client calling localhost:9000 in dev \u2014 the two docs disagree on the dev port."}, {"id": "keepqueue_server_readme_zod_validation", "label": "Zod Request Validation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "keepqueue-server/README.md", "source_location": "Tech Stack", "source_url": "https://keepqueue.com/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Validation is pushed to a middleware boundary so handlers can assume well-formed bodies, which matters more here because the cache-backed handlers write straight into shared in-memory state."}, {"id": "keepqueue_server_readme_firebase_backend", "label": "Firebase Backend (Firestore, Auth, Storage)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "keepqueue-server/README.md", "source_location": "Tech Stack", "source_url": "https://keepqueue.com/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Firebase is the single source of truth for data, identity and file storage; credentials are supplied through .env rather than checked-in service account files."}, {"id": "keepqueue_server_readme_api_routes", "label": "Server API Route Groups", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "keepqueue-server/README.md", "source_location": "API Routes", "source_url": "https://keepqueue.com/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three surfaces: / as a health check returning \"OK from root\", /actions for business actions and appointments, /data for read endpoints."}, {"id": "keepqueue_server_read